  "description": "Safe retries for POST and PATCH in Keel.Endpoints and any Minimal API: with an Idempotency-Key header, the first response is stored and retries get it back without running the handler again. Per-user keys, 422 on a reused key with another request, 409 while the first is still running. Stores in IDistributedCache (memory or Redis) or your own IIdempotencyStore.",
